[CHANGE] benchmark_4/parts/multi_interface/pretense/multi_interface_impl_pretense.py: Implemented StreamBuffer implementation pretense: pseudo-state machine inheriting StreamReaderStateMachine and StreamWriterStateMachine with call_target overrides for read/write/clear/unread_count/has_data/written_count asserting SUT postconditions, no state mutation or require_arg; TestStreamBufferImplReal lifecycle scenarios driven via as_checked; StreamBufferFuzzTest hypothesis suite with lifecycle-scoped make_sut; package-qualified imports.
[BLAME] benchmark_4/parts/multi_interface/pretense/multi_interface_impl_pretense.py: [slug:stream_writer.write.empty_payload] [viol:pret_qa.overspecified_oracle] Facet: empty payload write precondition Witness: payload='', call=StreamBuffer.write(''). The overridden write transition treats every generated string payload as a successful buffering write and asserts the written count increment, but stream_writer.write.empty_payload requires that an empty payload raise PayloadEmptyError and leave the buffer unchanged; the transition must model that contracted empty-payload branch by declaring the raise of PayloadEmptyError with no write-count increment (or otherwise gate the rule to non-empty payloads) so the state machine does not demand success for an empty payload.
[CHANGE] benchmark_4/parts/multi_interface/pretense/multi_interface_impl_pretense.py: Resolved empty-payload oracle feedback: StreamBuffer.write now models the contracted stream_writer.write.empty_payload branch explicitly, declaring the expected PayloadEmptyError around the call_target pivot for empty payloads and asserting the written count stays unchanged, while non-empty payloads keep the increment postcondition; removed over-specified all-strings-success assertion.
[BLAME] benchmark_4/parts/multi_interface/pretense/stream_writer_pretense.py: [slug:stream_writer.write.empty_payload] [viol:pret_qa.uncontracted_state_rule] Facet: empty payload write state model Witness: payload='', call=StreamWriter.write(''), modeled_items_delta=1. The write transition buffers every string payload into the modeled unread and written lists unconditionally, so an empty payload is recorded as a successful write even though stream_writer.write.empty_payload requires an empty payload to raise PayloadEmptyError and leave the buffer and written count unchanged; because the modeled lists then hold a payload the real stream never buffered, subsequent unread_count, written_count, has_data, and read assertions diverge from the SUT. The write transition must model the contracted empty-payload branch so the empty string is not appended to the modeled state (and the empty-payload contract is not silently treated as a successful buffering write).
[CHANGE] benchmark_4/parts/multi_interface/pretense/stream_writer_pretense.py: Resolved empty-payload state-model feedback: StreamWriter.write now evaluates its make_return_value pivot and returns immediately for an empty payload so nothing is appended to the modeled items/written lists, keeping model state and derived written_count/unread_count/has_data/read observations consistent with the SUT for the contracted empty-payload branch; seed_written sibling transition audited and given the same empty-payload guard.
[CHANGE] benchmark_4/parts/multi_interface/pretense/multi_interface_impl_pretense.py: Re-verified after the writer interface dependency change: the StreamBuffer write override already models the empty-payload precondition branch with an expected exception around the call_target pivot and asserts an unchanged written count, and the inherited writer model transition now guards its empty-payload state mutation; no further code change required.
